    "field": "Atmospheric blocking and climate variability",
    "problem": "Previous studies established a statistical correlation between atmospheric blocking and the NAO/PNA climate patterns, but the dynamical mechanisms and cause-effect relationships linking them remain poorly understood, partly due to methods that hamper direct dynamical analysis.",
    "method": "This study investigates the linkage between atmospheric blocking and NAO/PNA patterns by applying a PV-based blocking index, composite mapping, and EOF analysis to ERA-40 re-analysis data to examine their temporal and spatial correlations and the evolution of climate indices during blocking life-cycles.",
    "task": "The task is to explore the spatial and temporal linkage between atmospheric blocking and the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO) and Pacific-North American (PNA) patterns, examining their correlation and interrelationship using ERA-40 reanalysis data.",
